Basilisk Knights are a [[slayer]] creature that can be found in the [[Jormungand's Prison]] beneath the [[Island of Stone]], requiring level 60 [[Slayer]] and completion of [[The Fremennik Exiles]] to kill. Like [[cockatrice]] and [[basilisk]]s, players must equip a [[mirror shield]] or [[V's shield]] when fighting these monsters or they will take heavy damage and their stats will be drained.

The basilisk knight has an improved drop table from regular basilisks, and can drop the [[basilisk jaw]], which can be used to upgrade the [[helm of Neitiznot]] to the [[Neitiznot faceguard]].

==Requirements==
*Level {{SCP|Slayer|60}} to deal damage against the Basilisk Knights.
*Completion of {{SCP|Quest}} [[The Fremennik Exiles]] to access [[Jormungand's Prison]] on the [[Island of Stone]].

===Recommendations===
*High [[combat]] stats. Although not required, see the skill levels below for an indication of the advised stats:
**If using [[Melee]]:
***Level {{SCP|Attack|80}} or higher
***Level {{SCP|Strength|80}} or higher
***Level {{SCP|Defence|80}} or higher
***Level {{SCP|Hitpoints|80}} or higher
***Level {{SCP|Prayer|70}} or higher for the [[Piety]] prayer
**If using [[Ranged]]:
***Level {{SCP|Ranged|75}} or higher

==Transportation==
Make your way to the [[Rellekka]] north-western docks using one of the methods below:

* Teleport with [[Fremennik sea boots]]
* Use a [[Lunar isle teleport]] or portal in your [[player-owned house]], and speak to any citizen to get kicked off [[Lunar Isle]] to [[Rellekka]]
* Teleport to [[Waterbirth Island]] and ask [[Jarvald]] to ferry you directly to Rellekka
* Use an [[enchanted lyre]] to teleport to Waterbirth Island or Rellekka

Speak to [[Haskell]] at the most western dock to travel to the [[Island of Stone]]. Walk briefly north to find the entrance to [[Jormungand's Prison]]. Once inside this dungeon, travel briefly south-west to the room where the fight against [[The Jormungand]] took place during The Fremennik Exiles. It is now full of [[Basilisk Knight]]s.

==Mechanics==
===Attack styles===
Basilisk Knights use standard melee and magic attacks, both with a maximum hit of 20. 

While out of melee range, the Basilisk Knight's attacks become somewhat unusual. The knight will only retaliate with Magic whenever attacked by the player, or every 4 ticks if the player's weapon attack speed is faster.

===Improved drop rates on Slayer tasks===
The drop rate of a [[basilisk jaw]] is increased to 1/1,000 (from 1/5,000) while on a basilisk [[Slayer task]]. 

==Strategy==

=== Melee ===
When meleeing, it is recommended to use [[Protect from Magic]] at all times and tank their melee hits. Bring plenty of [[prayer potion|prayer potion]]s along with high-healing food, and [[super combat potion]]s. Thralls cannot be used, but [[Vengeance]] or [[Death charge]] may be helpful instead. Alternatively, runes for [[High Level Alchemy]] could be brought along with [[Telekinetic Grab]].

===Ranging===
Basilisk Knights can be easily safespotted due to their large size and the number of obstacles around the prison. Due to the need for [[V's shield]] and the weakness to [[heavy range]], crossbows are typically used.

It is possible to avoid all damage from the Basilisk Knights' melee attacks by utilising the [[Protect from Magic]] prayer and using a [[Ranged]] attack style out of melee distance. A good spot for this is just outside of the entryway to the room containing [[The Jormungand]], as they are unable to pass through the one-tile wide doorway and can only use magic attacks.

'''Note: Basilisk Knights will attempt to enter melee range once engaged in combat.''' Thus, it is essential that players always attack from a safespot where the knights cannot reach.

